6 Conclusion
In this paper, I quantify both the direct and indirect effects of the feebate policy and find that it increases global welfare. Consumers are worse off when they are taxed to subsidise the policy cost, but their loss is more than offset by an increase in the profits of French manufacturers. With a uniform tax rate, the feebate appears to favour the middle-income class, while it is progressive with a tax that is proportional to income. The policy decreases average
